# Ground card throw / stack (locked)

This system is working. Do not "improve" it with physics-rest poses, full-pile restacks, or extra Y gaps.

## Settle (WorldCard.FlattenAndSnapToGround)

- Always flatten: `LookRotation(ProjectOnPlane(transform.forward), up)`. Never leave a card upright.
- Keep landing yaw. Do **not** pick visual.up vs visual.right (that caused 90° drift and upside-down textures).
- Face up/down from `_cardVisual.forward.y` **before** rewriting rotation, then `groundShowsBack`.
- Then `ApplyStackHeight(this, placeOnTop: true)` once. Do not snap Y to floor first.

## Stack (CardGroundStack)

- Thrown card only: `PlaceOnTopOfOverlaps` — layer = max overlapping layer + 1. **Do not move other cards.**
- `StackStep` = card thickness × world scale (+ tiny z-fight epsilon). No large `StackGap`.
- `GetUniqueDepthBias` only on **layer 0** (scatter z-fight). Never add bias to stacked layers.
- Do not flood-fill restack the pile on throw or pickup. `RebuildAll` / cell piles are for 5000-card scatter spawn only.

## Pickup (CardGroundQuery)

- Math raycast, not thousands of colliders.
- If several overlapping cards are hit, pick the **highest GroundStackLayer**.
- Skip cards with `HasActivePhysics`. Remove Rigidbody immediately on settle (`DestroyImmediate`).

## Perf

- Settled ground cards stay GPU-instanced (front/back). Do not keep a mesh visual on every thrown card.
- Landing colliders are temporary (flight only), then restore trigger/off.
